      <div class="var-card"><div class="var-num">2</div><h3>Function-Focused Blueprint</h3><p>One or two columns elevated in detail — used when a specific team or initiative needs deeper clarity within the broader enterprise framework.</p><div class="var-examples">→ Akamai Seller 360, Akamai Workforce, Akamai S&OP</div></div>
      <div class="var-card"><div class="var-num">3</div><h3>Industry-Specific Blueprint</h3><p>Columns and metrics tailored to a vertical's unique operating model — HESS for energy, EEV/EVA for insurance, yield metrics for semiconductors.</p><div class="var-examples">→ Symetra, Oil & Gas, GlobalFoundries, VISA</div></div>
      <div class="var-card"><div class="var-num">4</div><h3>Technology-Connected Blueprint</h3><p>Extends the grid to show plan types, data sources, and system connections — bridging strategy directly to EPM implementation.</p><div class="var-examples">→ Columbia Distributing, ADM-Hyperion</div></div>
      <div class="var-card"><div class="var-num">5</div><h3>Imperative-Led Blueprint</h3><p>Corporate strategic imperatives explicitly anchored at the top, with lines of impact drawn down into functional metrics — reinforcing accountability.</p><div class="var-examples">→ Family Dollar (2023 Imperatives), Bell Bank</div></div>
      <div class="var-card"><div class="var-num">6</div><h3>Periodic Table Format</h3><p>An alternative visual using the Business Foundation "Periodic Table" style — element-tile layout for clients who prefer a modular, non-grid presentation.</p><div class="var-examples">→ Apple, Citrix, ADM</div></div>
